= <span style="color: #C0A054;">**DVP**</span> Congress

Amidst the growing appeal of special interests, the atrophication of the <span style="color: #C0A054;">**DVP’s**</span> vote and the ailing health of Streseman, there is a renewed impetus for him to secure his party’s future. This might be his very last chance to influence the yearslong struggle for control of the <span style="color: #C0A054;">**DVP**</span>.

Spearheaded by the white collar representatives of the <span style="color: #a2c617;">DHV</span> and supported by Stresemann, the left wing of the <span style="color: #C0A054;">**DVP**</span> has introduced a reform which aims to give working and middle class elements more influence in the <span style="color: #C0A054;">**DVP**</span>, thus weakening the leverage of the industrialists on the right. This would finally free the <span style="color: #C0A054;">**DVP**</span> from the reactionary social policies of heavy industry, enabling it to become a true volkspartei rather than one governed by parochial interests. Ultimately, the results of this will determine the course of the <span style="color: #C0A054;">**DVP**</span> for the years to come. 

- @resultsdvp: The party votes...

@resultsdvp
go-to: left if stresemann_reform_yay; right if stresemann_reform_nay; left_conflict if stresemann_reform_mid

@reform_pass
on-arrival: dvp_left += 10; dvp_relation += 5; liberal_cooperation += 3; workers_dvp += 1; workers_other -= 1; new_middle_dvp += 4; new_middle_other -= 4; old_middle_dvp += 4; old_middle_other -= 4; rural_dvp += 2; rural_other -= 2; catholics_other -= 2; catholics_z -= 2; catholics_dvp += 4; coalition_dissent -= 2 if in_grand_coalition; dvp_reform = 1; pro_republic += 5; ddp_left += 1.5; ddp_cohesion += 1.5; rdi_balance -= 5; 

With his continued threats of resignation and backed by a coalition of the remaining constructive elements of the <span style="color: #C0A054;">**DVP**</span>, Stresemann has managed to push through the organisational reform by a slim margin. As a result, the ability of the industrialists to garner advantageous positions for their representatives on the national list has been severely limited. Not willing to abandon their influence in the <span style="color: #C0A054;">**DVP**</span> so quickly, donations from heavy industry will continue, albeit at a slower pace. Nevertheless, the <span style="color: #C0A054;">**DVP**</span> will continue on its leftwards pro-republican path for now, which has advanced the cause for liberal unity. 

@reform_fail
on-arrival: dvp_right += 5; dvp_relation -= 3; coalition_dissent += 1 if in_grand_coalition; old_middle_dnvp += 2; new_middle_dnvp += 2; dvp_reform = 0; pro_republic -= 3; ddp_right += 1; ddp_cohesion -= 1; rdi_balance += 8; 

Following the recent elections, the industrialist forces in the <span style="color: #C0A054;">**DVP’s**</span> Reichstag delegation have been greatly strengthened, in part due to their monetary contributions to the <span style="color: #C0A054;">**DVP’s**</span> diminished coffers.  [? if dnvp_leader == “Hugenberg” : Furthermore, with Hugenberg’s leadership of the DNVP, many industrialists have shifted to the <span style="color: #C0A054;">**DVP**</span> and entrenched themselves on the party’s right. ?] Thus, they have overwhelmingly rejected the reform and have passed a resolution to allow the Reichstag delegation independence from the demands of the Central Committee. This has severely weakened Stresemann’s hold over the party, instead benefitting Ernst Scholz, Reichstag delegation leader and a key figure on the party’s right.

